-- ============================================================================
-- PD3 ASSOCIATE DEEP SEED: ESP Design, beginner tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: THE STAGE. An electric submersible pump is a stack of
-- identical stages, and every number about the stack is the stage's number
-- multiplied by a count. So the whole design rests on three published curves
-- through five catalogue points, and this tier is about how far those curves
-- can be trusted.
--
-- THE TIER IS BUILT ON ONE SENTENCE: `inRange: false` IS A FLAG ON THE ANSWER,
-- NOT A REFUSAL. The golden itself carries a row 1300 bbl/d past the end of
-- the published data, returning 0.052063 ft of head and 0.004291 hp from a
-- cubic that was never asked to stop. On a whole design it is larger:
-- `sizePump` at 40 Hz, the golden's own lowest tested frequency, returns 926
-- stages off a stage making 3.9802 ft, 5.58 times the design pump, with three
-- warnings and no refusal.
--
-- AND NOTHING SNAPS. Head does not go negative until 36.1016 Hz, six and a
-- half Hz below where the answers stopped meaning anything, and the only hard
-- stop in the whole chain, `stageCount` refusing a non-positive head per
-- stage, fires 1306.6229 bbl/d after that. Every number degrades smoothly and
-- the boolean is the only field that changes at the boundary. The flag also
-- carries no DISTANCE: it reads identical 100 bbl/d out and 1300 bbl/d out.
-- A learner who expects a numerical method to announce its own failure is the
-- learner this tier exists for.
--
-- TWO THINGS THE TIER MUST NOT OVERSTATE, and both are in the lessons.
-- `bepOf` is a 400 step SCAN and not a solve, so the best efficiency rate is
-- quantised to 5.0000 bbl/d on the vendor curve and the four reference stages
-- all miss their own generating rates. Say scanned, not found. And `region`
-- is defined two different ways: outside the published range it comes from the
-- range alone, inside it from the 0.75 to 1.25 band around the best efficiency
-- point, so "upthrust" on an extrapolated reading and "upthrust" on an
-- in-range reading are not the same statement and the field does not
-- distinguish them.
--
-- THE QUALITY CHECK CANNOT CATCH THE ERROR CLASS IT EXISTS FOR. `fitStageCurve`
-- warns on head RMSE alone, and the wave's teaching curve carries a deliberate
-- one decimal transcription slip that takes the fit RMSE from 0.05345225 to
-- 0.58797473 ft, a tenfold degradation, and passes the 2 percent bar silently.
-- An aggregate hides one bad point among four good ones, which is exactly the
-- shape of a transcription error.
--
-- The only numbers that travel from this tier to the next are the curve itself
-- and the frequency it was published at.
-- ============================================================================

values ('esp', 'beginner', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-a-stack-of-stages","title":"A Stack of Stages","lesson_keys":["l01-what-an-esp-is","l02-what-this-engine-models","l03-what-it-refuses","l04-the-curves-that-define-a-stage"]},{"key":"m02-fitting-a-curve","title":"Fitting a Curve","lesson_keys":["l01-three-curves-one-stage","l02-the-cubic-fit","l03-how-good-is-the-fit","l04-reading-head-at-a-rate","l05-what-a-fit-assumes"]},{"key":"m03-the-best-efficiency-point","title":"The Best Efficiency Point","lesson_keys":["l01-what-bep-is","l02-finding-it","l03-the-operating-range","l04-what-bep-does-not-promise"]},{"key":"m04-the-duty-point","title":"The Duty Point","lesson_keys":["l01-head-at-duty","l02-efficiency-at-duty","l03-power-per-stage","l04-three-readings-one-point","l05-what-a-duty-point-cannot-tell-you"]},{"key":"m05-outside-the-data","title":"Outside the Data","lesson_keys":["l01-a-flag-is-not-a-refusal","l02-a-cubic-beyond-its-data","l03-where-head-goes-negative","l04-what-an-unbounded-fit-costs","l05-reading-a-warning"]},{"key":"m06-the-associate-reading","title":"The Associate Reading","lesson_keys":["l01-the-story-so-far","l02-working-the-capstone","l03-onward"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
on conflict (app_slug, tier) do update
  set structure = excluded.structure,
      content_version = excluded.content_version,
      active = true,
      updated_at = now();

delete from public.academy_quiz_questions
 where app_slug = 'esp' and tier = 'beginner';

